  "documentation": {
    "range": "Range includes humid lowlands on the Atlantic versant from eastern Honduras to western Panama and on the Pacific versant in southwestern Costa Rica and adjacent Panama. In Costa Rica, this species is also found in the premontane zone of Río Reventazón valley, in the central area of the country (Savage 2002). Elevational range extends from near sea level to 775 meters (Wilson and Johnson<span style=\"font-style: italic;\"></span> 2010).",
    "population": "It is a very common species in good habitat.",
    "habitats": "Habitats of this diurnal, semiaquatic, semiarboreal species include stream courses with considerable stands of trees still intact in Lowland Moist and Wet Forests and into Premontane Wet Forest (Savage 2002). It is an egg-laying species.",
    "threats": "This species is threatened by a loss of primary forest habitat resulting from the the impacts of expanding human populations.",
    "measures": "It is found in some protected areas. There is a need to monitor the harvesting of this species for the pet trade, although at present this does not appear to be a major threat (many in the trade are captive bred).",
    "use_trade": "It has been recorded in the pet trade.",
    "rationale": "Listed as Least Concern in view of its wide range, large overall population, and because it is not declining fast enough to qualify for a threatened category.",
    "trend_justification": null,
    "taxonomic_notes": null
  },
